.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
.Dd November 12, 2026
.Dt NOQTIS-DATA 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm noqtis-data
.Nd the noqtis data record, noqtis-data-1
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A data record is the file
.Pa noqtis.data.json
at the top of a capsule folder
.Pq Xr noqtis-capsule 5 .
It says where each data file of the capsule came from, what shape it
has, how it was summarised, and what was done and checked with it.
The record is an ordinary file of the capsule: the manifest lists it
with its digests and the seal covers it, so
.Xr noqtis-check 1
fails when it changes, and
.Xr noqtis-data 1
.Pq Cm noqtis data check
checks the files against what it says.
.Pp
The key words MUST, MUST NOT, SHOULD and MAY are to be read as in
RFC 2119 and RFC 8174.
.Ss Canonical JSON
The record MUST be JSON (RFC 8259) in the canonical form of RFC 8785:
UTF-8, no whitespace outside strings, object members sorted by the
UTF-16 code units of their names, the minimal string escapes, and
numbers as IEEE 754 doubles in the shortest form that round-trips, as
ECMAScript writes them.
A reader MUST reject a record that is not byte-identical to its own
canonical form, has a duplicate member name, a string with U+0000 or
not valid UTF-8, a number that is not finite, objects nested deeper
than 32 levels, or more than 64 MiB.
The same record is therefore the same bytes whichever program wrote it.
.Ss Types
.Bl -tag -width "count"
.It string
at most 65,536 bytes.
.It path
a string naming a file of the capsule as the manifest does: relative,
.Ql /
between folders, no empty,
.Ql \&.
or
.Ql \&..
segment, no backslash, colon or control character, at most 4,096
bytes, and not
.Pa noqtis.json ,
.Pa noqtis.sig ,
.Pa noqtis.ers
or
.Pa noqtis.data.json .
.It hex
64 lower-case hex digits.
.It count
a whole number from 0 to 2^53.
.It time
.Ql YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ ,
a valid UTC time.
.It date
.Ql YYYY-MM-DD ,
a valid date of the proleptic Gregorian calendar.
.El
.Ss The record
An object with
.Cm format ,
the string
.Ql noqtis-data-1 ,
and any of the members below; no other member.
A reader MUST reject a member it does not know, so that a record of a
later format is refused rather than half-read.
Arrays keyed by
.Cm path
.Pq Cm sources , schemas , stats
or
.Cm name
.Pq Cm checks
MUST be sorted by the bytes of the key, with no key twice;
.Cm steps
and
.Cm commits
keep the order they were written in.
An array of objects MUST NOT be empty: a member with nothing in it is
left out, so that each record has one form.
.Bl -tag -width "commits"
.It Cm sources
Where each file came from.
Each element:
.Cm path
(path, required),
.Cm sha256
(hex, required: the file's SHA-256),
.Cm size
(count, required: its size in bytes),
and optionally
.Cm url
(where it was fetched),
.Cm resolver
(an object:
.Cm kind ,
one of
.Ql direct ,
.Ql ckan ,
.Ql socrata ,
.Ql arcgis ,
.Ql wayback ,
required; and the strings
.Cm base
(the portal),
.Cm id
(the dataset),
.Cm resource ,
.Cm format ,
and the count
.Cm layer ) ,
.Cm retrieved
(time),
.Cm etag ,
.Cm modified
(the server's ETag and Last-Modified, as sent),
.Cm licence ,
.Cm publisher ,
.Cm title
(strings),
.Cm archived
(an object: the archived copy's
.Cm url ,
required, and its
.Cm time ) ,
.Cm mirrors
(an array of URLs with the same bytes),
.Cm synthetic
(true when the file is a generated stand-in for the real data; every
report line about it says so).
.It Cm schemas
The shape of a CSV file.
Each element:
.Cm path
(required),
.Cm kind
(required:
.Ql csv ) ,
.Cm delim
(one byte, not a quote or line break; default
.Ql \&, ) ,
.Cm header
(boolean; default true),
.Cm na
(an array of strings that mean a missing value; default
.Ql ""
and
.Ql NA ) ,
.Cm rows
(an object with counts
.Cm min
and
.Cm max ) ,
.Cm columns
and
.Cm rules .
.Pp
.Cm columns
lists the columns in file order, each with
.Cm name
(required, no name twice),
.Cm type
(required:
.Ql int ,
.Ql real ,
.Ql text ,
.Ql date
or
.Ql bool ) ,
.Cm nulls
(boolean: whether a missing value is allowed; default true),
.Cm min
and
.Cm max
(numbers for
.Ql int
and
.Ql real ,
dates for
.Ql date ) ,
and
.Cm set
(for
.Ql text :
the values allowed).
.Pp
.Cm rules
are checks over a column or the table, each with
.Cm kind
and its arguments:
.Ql unique
.Pq Cm col No or Cm cols : No no value, or combination, twice ,
.Ql notnull
.Pq Cm col ,
.Ql range
.Pq Cm col , Cm min No and/or Cm max ,
.Ql set
.Pq Cm col , Cm set ,
.Ql incr
.Pq Cm col : No each value at least the one before ,
.Ql complete
.Pq Cm col , Cm share : No at least that share not missing ,
.Ql distinct
.Pq Cm col , Cm min No and/or Cm max No distinct values ,
.Ql rows
and
.Ql cols
.Pq Cm min No and/or Cm max .
.It Cm stats
Summaries kept to detect drift later without keeping the data
.Pq Xr noqtis-drift 1 .
Each element:
.Cm path
(required),
.Cm rows
(count, required) and
.Cm columns ,
each with
.Cm name
and
.Cm n
(required: the values not missing),
.Cm nulls ,
and for a numeric column
.Cm q
(the quantile sketch: [value, count] pairs, value increasing, count
the number of values at most it),
.Cm edges
and
.Cm counts
(the binning of the population stability index: increasing interior
edges, bins closed on the right, one count more than edges),
.Cm digits
(nine counts of first significant digits 1 to 9);
for a categorical column
.Cm cats
([value, count] pairs sorted by value) and
.Cm other
(the count of values beyond those kept).
.Xr noqtis-drift 1
defines how they are made and the error of each test made from them.
.It Cm env
The environment of the run: strings
.Cm os ,
.Cm arch ,
.Cm kernel ,
.Cm cpu ,
.Cm locale ,
.Cm tz ,
.Cm noqtis ,
.Cm build ;
.Cm runtime
(an object:
.Cm language
required,
.Cm version ,
.Cm packages ,
an array of
.Brq Cm name , Cm version , Cm source
sorted by name);
.Cm locks
(lock files: an array of
.Brq Cm path , Cm sha256
sorted by path);
.Cm rng
(an object:
.Cm kind
required, and
.Cm seed ,
a number or string).
.It Cm steps
What was done to the data, in order: each with
.Cm kind
(required:
.Ql recode ,
.Ql filter ,
.Ql derive ,
.Ql script
or
.Ql other ) ,
and the strings
.Cm from ,
.Cm to ,
.Cm note ,
.Cm script
(a path) and
.Cm sha256
(of a mapping or script).
.It Cm checks
Results of checks made elsewhere (a published total, a falsification
test): each with
.Cm name
(required),
.Cm status
(required:
.Ql pass ,
.Ql warn
or
.Ql fail ) ,
.Cm expected
and
.Cm observed
(a number or string),
.Cm tol
(a number) and
.Cm note .
A check recorded as
.Ql fail
fails its row in
.Cm noqtis data check .
.It Cm commits
Sealed commitments (a randomisation list, a pre-registration): each with
.Cm kind
(required:
.Ql randomisation ,
.Ql preregistration
or
.Ql other ) ,
.Cm created
(time, required),
.Cm alg
(required:
.Ql sha3-256 ) ,
.Cm digest
(hex, required),
.Cm after
(time: not to be revealed before) and
.Cm label .
.It Cm cite
How to cite the data: an object with
.Cm title
(required),
.Cm authors
(an array of strings),
.Cm version ,
.Cm doi ,
.Cm url ,
.Cm licence
and the count
.Cm year .
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal
{"format":"noqtis-data-1","sources":[{"licence":"OGL-Canada-2.0",
"path":"data/a.csv","publisher":"City of Example",
"retrieved":"2026-01-01T00:00:00Z","sha256":"7a1668480cde19db0b76c7a36e6
fee9a82afd9937f5d03cec3dae1705ce173e2","size":89,
"url":"https://example.org/a.csv"}]}
.Ed
.Pp
(one line in the file; broken here to fit).
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr noqtis-data 1 ,
.Xr nqdchk 3 ,
.Xr nqdnew 3 ,
.Xr noqtis-capsule 5
